cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "twilight: a Monte Carlo radiative-transfer simulator of the twilight sky with a validated model of human dawn and dusk visibility"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Mahdi"
    given-names: "Mostafa"
    email: "me@mostafa.dk"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Muno459/twilight"
url: "https://github.com/Muno459/twilight"
license: "MIT OR Apache-2.0"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-05"
keywords:
  - radiative transfer
  - Monte Carlo
  - twilight
  - sky brightness
  - atmospheric optics
  - visual detection
  - prayer times
  - fajr
abstract: >-
  twilight computes absolute spectral sky radiance through deep twilight by
  backward Monte Carlo radiative transfer in a spherical refracting
  atmosphere, with measured 3D cloud fields, full Stokes polarization, and
  every celestial and artificial background light source. The transport is
  validated against DISORT, MYSTIC (to 1e9 photons), SHDOM, and measured
  twilight skies. A psychophysical detection layer, validated against
  sixteen published human dawn-observation campaigns, computes the Quranic
  dawn and dusk events (Fajr and Isha) as visual detection times with
  propagated uncertainties. A methods and validation paper is in
  preparation; until it appears, please cite this repository.
